    },
    {
      "text": "Figure 10: Closer look at comparison of algorithms in Safety PyBullet DroneCircle and BallRun Environments.",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        392.6667785644531,
        504.0037841796875,
        400.6827392578125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "RESPO: In the both BallRun and DroneCircle, our approach achieves the highest or among the",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        415.7027893066406,
        503.99688720703125,
        424.7289123535156
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "highest reward performance compared to the other safety baselines. Furthermore, RESPO converges",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        426.6117858886719,
        504.0018310546875,
        435.6379089355469
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "to almost 0 constraint violations for both environments.",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        437.48095703125,
        328.9899597167969,
        446.5469055175781
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "PPOLag: In DroneCircle, PPOLag has the best reward performance. Although its costs violations",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        453.9097900390625,
        504.0008850097656,
        462.9359130859375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "are around the cost threshold, it is much higher than RESPO. On the other hand, in BallRun, PPOLag",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        464.81878662109375,
        504.0003967285156,
        473.84490966796875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "has very low reward performance.",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        475.84735107421875,
        243.63082885742188,
        484.75390625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "RCRL: We again see RCRL take on behavior with extremes – it has low reward and cost violations",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        492.11578369140625,
        503.99786376953125,
        501.14190673828125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "in Drone Circle and has high reward and cost violations in BallRun. Constraining the maximum",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        503.14434814453125,
        503.9972229003906,
        512.0509033203125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "violation with the reachability value function as RCRL does seems to provide poor safety in an",
      "bbox": [
        107.7509994506836,
        513.9337768554688,
        503.9990539550781,
        522.9598999023438
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "environment with non-tangible constraints (i.e. a speed limit in BallRun).",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        524.96240234375,
        400.42218017578125,
        533.8689575195312
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "FAC: While in BallRun, we see FAC have the same low reward and low violations behavior,",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        541.2318115234375,
        505.2401428222656,
        550.2579345703125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "DroneCircle shows an instance where FAC can achieve decently high rewards while maintaining low",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        552.1408081054688,
        504.3608093261719,
        561.1669311523438
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "violations.",
      "bbox": [
        107.7509994506836,
        563.1693725585938,
        149.54409790039062,
        572.075927734375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "CBF: In DroneCircle, the CBF approach has low rewards and relatively low violations; in BallRun,",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        579.4387817382812,
        505.24151611328125,
        588.4649047851562
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "it has a bit higher rewards compared to all the low performance algorithms with very low violations.",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        590.4673461914062,
        505.74566650390625,
        599.3739013671875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "CRPO, P3O, & PCPO: These CMDP-based primal approaches have mediocre reward performance",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        606.7357788085938,
        503.9972839355469,
